WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:16.820
It's two plus two
equals six.


00:02:19.354 --> 00:02:21.691
I will never tell you.


00:02:21.721 --> 00:02:22.893
But you will.


00:02:23.031 --> 00:02:28.228
OPERATION DUNKIRK


00:02:29.191 --> 00:02:32.691
Subrip: Pix
<font color=#ff0000>subs4free.info</font>


00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.173
<i>The enemy attacked us
on all sides</i>


00:03:06.203 --> 00:03:08.775
<i>with great strength
and fierceness.</i>


00:03:08.805 --> 00:03:11.745
<i>Pressing in upon
the narrow exit,</i>


00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:13.947
<i>both from the east
and from the west,</i>


00:03:13.977 --> 00:03:17.183
<i>the enemy began
to fire with cannon</i>


00:03:17.213 --> 00:03:19.816
<i>upon the beaches by
which alone the shipping</i>


00:03:19.846 --> 00:03:22.588
<i>could approach or depart.</i>


00:03:22.618 --> 00:03:25.672
<i>Meanwhile, the Royal Navy
with the willing help</i>


00:03:25.702 --> 00:03:28.757
<i>of countless Merchant
Seamen strained</i>


00:03:28.758 --> 00:03:33.796
<i>every nerve to embark
the British and Allied troops.</i>


00:03:33.826 --> 00:03:37.037
<i>Two-hundred and twenty light
warships</i>


00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:41.275
<i>and 650 other vessels
were engaged.</i>


00:03:41.305 --> 00:03:43.840
<i>They had to operate
upon a difficult coast</i>


00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:47.246
<i>often in adverse weather</i>


00:03:47.276 --> 00:03:51.214
<i>under an almost
ceaseless hail of bombs</i>


00:03:51.215 --> 00:03:55.485
<i>and an increasing concentration
of artillery fire.</i>


00:03:55.515 --> 00:03:57.824
<i>Nor were the seas,
as I have said,</i>


00:03:57.854 --> 00:04:00.926
<i>themselves free
from mines and torpedoes.</i>


00:04:00.956 --> 00:04:03.492
<i>It was in conditions
such as these that our men</i>


00:04:03.522 --> 00:04:06.912
<i>carried on with
little or no rest.</i>


00:04:06.942 --> 00:04:10.303
<i>For days and nights on end,</i>


00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:14.340
<i>making trip after trip
across the dangerous waters,</i>


00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.608
<i>bringing with them always
men whom they had rescued.</i>


00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:43.550
Attention!


00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.604
At ease.


00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:48.474
Lt. Calloway?


00:04:48.504 --> 00:04:51.192
This must be your lucky day.


00:04:51.222 --> 00:04:53.881
You're not being evacuated.


00:04:53.911 --> 00:04:56.831
You might actually
live another day.


00:04:56.861 --> 00:04:59.675
It's a ruddy
bloodbath out there!


00:04:59.705 --> 00:05:02.489
Gentlemen, battles
will be won


00:05:02.519 --> 00:05:05.120
by the side that
first spots enemy airplanes,


00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.159
ships or submarines.


00:05:07.189 --> 00:05:09.526
And British scientists have
been working feverishly


00:05:09.556 --> 00:05:12.561
to develop radar
technology that will see


00:05:12.591 --> 00:05:15.597
for hundreds of miles,
even at night.


00:05:15.598 --> 00:05:19.304
But they haven't been
able to crack it.


00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:21.837
Just recently, we got
intelligence from the Americans.


00:05:21.838 --> 00:05:23.306
The Americans?


00:05:23.336 --> 00:05:24.643
Yes.


00:05:24.673 --> 00:05:27.476
Seems a German scientist
has developed this technology


00:05:27.506 --> 00:05:30.279
but doesn't want
to share it with Hitler.


00:05:30.309 --> 00:05:32.184
I know.


00:05:32.214 --> 00:05:34.253
Whatever his reasons,
he wants to share it with us.


00:05:34.283 --> 00:05:38.788
Therefore, I need you and your
men to go retrieve the package.


00:05:38.818 --> 00:05:40.856
The package being?


00:05:40.857 --> 00:05:42.794
The German scientist.


00:05:42.824 --> 00:05:44.729
Do we know where this
package is, sir?


00:05:44.759 --> 00:05:46.898
Yes. We're being told
the French Resistance has


00:05:46.928 --> 00:05:50.332
the German scientist in a
safe house not far from here.


00:05:50.333 --> 00:05:55.706
He's being held here
in an old factory


00:05:55.736 --> 00:05:58.410
right off of L'Autoroute A25.


00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.179
That's 51 degrees north,
37 east.


00:06:01.209 --> 00:06:04.079
You're to go there,
rendezvous with the French,


00:06:04.109 --> 00:06:06.915
retrieve the package,
and get out.


00:06:06.945 --> 00:06:08.354
Any questions?


00:06:08.384 --> 00:06:10.687
Much enemy activity
in the area, sir?


00:06:10.717 --> 00:06:13.039
From our reports,
little to none.


00:06:13.069 --> 00:06:15.391
The French are
expecting you.


00:06:15.421 --> 00:06:17.296
Once you've made contact,


00:06:17.326 --> 00:06:19.528
they will ask you for
a piece of paper.


00:06:19.558 --> 00:06:21.730
Give them this.


00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:23.236
Sir.


00:06:23.266 --> 00:06:24.970
Any more questions?


00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.204
So we're not going to be
evacuated, then. Is that it?


00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.873
You have your orders.


00:06:30.874 --> 00:06:34.210
Pull your balls out of your
throat and be a soldier!


00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.111
- Yes, sir!
- Get your kit together


00:06:36.112 --> 00:06:38.382
and get ready to move out.
Do you understand me?


00:06:38.412 --> 00:06:39.483
Yes, sir!


00:06:41.384 --> 00:06:45.588
This mission could
not only save lives,


00:06:45.618 --> 00:06:47.057
but win the war.


00:06:48.925 --> 00:06:51.028
Carry on.


00:07:02.137 --> 00:07:04.106
You heard the colonel.


00:07:04.107 --> 00:07:06.242
Little to no enemy activity.


00:07:06.272 --> 00:07:07.313
We get in, we get out.


00:07:07.343 --> 00:07:09.482
We don't miss the evacuation.


00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:12.281
Just one last roll
of the dice, lads.


00:07:17.519 --> 00:07:18.621
Let's go.


00:08:14.943 --> 00:08:17.764
Should be just over
this field.


00:08:17.794 --> 00:08:20.616
Better proceed
with caution.


00:09:05.294 --> 00:09:07.197
Into the bushes!


00:09:45.467 --> 00:09:48.471
You must love your
family very much, no?


00:09:50.472 --> 00:09:52.475
Do you realize that
we know where they are?


00:09:54.277 --> 00:09:58.948
My soldiers are on their way
right now to pick them up.


00:09:58.978 --> 00:10:02.852
<i>Mein familia has
nothing to do with this!</i>


00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.634
No!


00:10:25.251 --> 00:10:28.588
Tell me!


00:10:46.714 --> 00:10:50.087
Okay.
Okay.


00:10:50.117 --> 00:10:53.289
I give it
to a young woman,


00:10:53.319 --> 00:10:58.825
French Resistance
on her way to BAF now.


00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:09.436
Angelique!


00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.243
Show me where she is.


00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:40.800
They will see you
soon enough.


00:12:16.596 --> 00:12:18.433
Everything all right, Thomas?


00:12:18.463 --> 00:12:21.200
It's my son's birthday
in two weeks.


00:12:21.201 --> 00:12:24.573
I just really
wanted to see him.


00:12:24.603 --> 00:12:28.541
I haven't seen him
yet since he was born.


00:12:31.276 --> 00:12:32.711
Don't worry about it,
Thomas.


00:12:32.712 --> 00:12:35.867
You'll see him on his
next birthday, yeah?


00:12:35.897 --> 00:12:38.510
You can tell him what
a hero his father is.


00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.154
Never actually been
with a woman myself.


00:12:41.184 --> 00:12:43.088
You never been with a woman?


00:12:43.118 --> 00:12:45.157
Not intimately, no.


00:12:45.158 --> 00:12:47.828
So you've not had a shag?


00:12:47.858 --> 00:12:50.529
Such a romantic, Walker.


00:12:55.034 --> 00:12:56.273
Let's just find this kraut,


00:12:56.303 --> 00:12:58.505
and get the hell
out of France, yeah?


00:12:58.535 --> 00:13:00.275
What do you say?


00:13:00.305 --> 00:13:03.210
I hate this country.
It stinks.


00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.115
Lieutenant, all due respect,


00:13:06.145 --> 00:13:08.914
how do we know we can
trust this scientist?


00:13:08.944 --> 00:13:11.687
He is German, after all.


00:13:11.717 --> 00:13:15.053
Because cleverer men
than us have told us so.


00:13:15.083 --> 00:13:17.122
Well, they better be right.


00:13:19.058 --> 00:13:20.994
This must be it, lads.


00:13:24.329 --> 00:13:25.431
Stay sharp.


00:13:49.789 --> 00:13:51.609
Drop your weapons!


00:13:51.639 --> 00:13:55.894
Lower your guns!


00:13:55.895 --> 00:13:57.831
I said drop your guns!


00:13:57.861 --> 00:13:59.798
Turn!


00:13:59.799 --> 00:14:01.134
Turn slowly to me!


00:14:05.704 --> 00:14:06.742
Turn slowly!


00:14:06.772 --> 00:14:08.474
What is your business here?


00:14:10.343 --> 00:14:13.213
We're with the British
Expeditionary Force.


00:14:13.243 --> 00:14:15.531
We've come
to collect a package.


00:14:15.561 --> 00:14:17.850
You should have
a package for me.


00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.352
Yes. Yes, I do.


00:14:35.568 --> 00:14:36.606
Read it.


00:14:36.636 --> 00:14:38.805
Read it to me!


00:14:43.309 --> 00:14:45.729
"The children long
to play in the fields


00:14:45.759 --> 00:14:48.150
but had to settle
instead for the sand


00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.350
which was accompanied
by an enormous roar."


00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.586
All right, where is he?


00:14:54.587 --> 00:14:56.924
How many are with you?


00:14:56.954 --> 00:14:59.292
Just the five of us.


00:15:02.027 --> 00:15:03.829
All right, where is he?


00:15:03.859 --> 00:15:06.499
She is inside.


00:15:08.834 --> 00:15:11.469
Wait. She?


00:15:12.705 --> 00:15:14.173
You did not know.


00:15:14.174 --> 00:15:16.275
No. I thought we were
collecting the chap


00:15:16.305 --> 00:15:19.127
with the algorithm
for radar.


00:15:19.157 --> 00:15:21.938
You were until
he was captured


00:15:21.968 --> 00:15:24.749
by Nazi but moments
before this.


00:15:24.779 --> 00:15:25.951
He gave the algorithm.


00:15:25.981 --> 00:15:27.285
To Angelique.


00:15:27.286 --> 00:15:28.954
Angelique?


00:15:30.256 --> 00:15:33.927
<i>- Oui.
- All right, let's go.</i>


00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.991
Angelique?


00:16:03.021 --> 00:16:04.160
<i>C'est moi, Pierre.</i>


00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.727
Don't shoot, don't shoot.


00:16:07.757 --> 00:16:10.500
This is her.


00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.700
You have the algorithm?


00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.833
<i>- Oui.
- May I see it?</i>


00:16:14.834 --> 00:16:18.404
I have not written it down.
So you must keep me alive.


00:16:18.434 --> 00:16:20.038
Very sensible.


00:16:20.039 --> 00:16:21.741
Then we should leave.


00:16:21.771 --> 00:16:22.979
What's the plan?


00:16:23.009 --> 00:16:25.612
We must get her
to this location.


00:16:25.642 --> 00:16:27.346
They will further assist her.


00:16:27.347 --> 00:16:31.050
They have arranged a plane
to take her to Great Britain.


00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:35.788
But we must wait
for the Americans.


00:16:35.818 --> 00:16:37.726
They're already late.


00:16:37.756 --> 00:16:39.358
So I'm assuming the worst.


00:16:39.388 --> 00:16:40.560
We need to move.


00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.330
Shit! We've got company!


00:16:47.032 --> 00:16:49.636
So much for little
to no enemy activity.


00:16:49.666 --> 00:16:50.807
Take cover.


00:16:50.837 --> 00:16:52.623
I'll see if I
can delay them.


00:16:52.653 --> 00:16:54.409
All right,
let's dig in, lads.


00:16:54.439 --> 00:16:57.108
We were given a mission
and I plan on completing it.


00:16:57.138 --> 00:16:59.044
Harris, get me the colonel
on the wireless.


00:16:59.074 --> 00:17:00.282
Yes, sir.


00:17:00.312 --> 00:17:04.251
F13C here.
Come in, Dunkirk.


00:17:04.281 --> 00:17:08.221
F13C.
This is Colonel Plummer.


00:17:08.251 --> 00:17:10.056
Sir, I have the colonel.


00:17:13.393 --> 00:17:15.995
We're at the destination, sir.
But the package isn't here.


00:17:16.025 --> 00:17:17.433
<i>There is a French girl
with the Resistance.</i>


00:17:17.463 --> 00:17:19.531
<i>Said she was given
the algorithm by the scientist</i>


00:17:19.561 --> 00:17:21.466
<i>before he was captured
by the Nazis.</i>


00:17:21.496 --> 00:17:23.334
<i>Has she showed it to you?</i>


00:17:23.335 --> 00:17:25.805
Says she has it
memorized, sir.


00:17:25.835 --> 00:17:27.242
Blood hell!


00:17:27.272 --> 00:17:28.675
That changes things.


00:17:28.705 --> 00:17:30.078
One more thing, sir.


00:17:30.108 --> 00:17:31.577
We also appear
to have company.


00:17:31.607 --> 00:17:32.815
How many?


00:17:32.845 --> 00:17:34.316
Difficult to say.


00:17:34.346 --> 00:17:36.284
Looks like a transport
heading our way.


00:17:36.314 --> 00:17:38.884
Get your asses out of there
before they arrive!


00:17:38.885 --> 00:17:40.088
<i>Those are your orders!</i>


00:17:40.118 --> 00:17:42.554
Understood, sir.
F13C out.


00:17:45.223 --> 00:17:46.927
You don't trust me?


00:17:46.957 --> 00:17:48.661
They've arrived!


00:17:59.105 --> 00:18:03.076
It's the Germans.
On the left and right.


00:18:15.053 --> 00:18:17.589
We know you are in there!


00:18:17.619 --> 00:18:18.724
Come out!


00:19:18.416 --> 00:19:20.822
She's in there right now.


00:19:20.852 --> 00:19:25.657
Yes, sir, but she has been
joined by five BAF soldiers.


00:19:32.698 --> 00:19:34.266
And they are
in there right now?


00:19:34.296 --> 00:19:35.870
Are you sure?


00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:39.737
Yes, sir. They just arrived
maybe four or five minutes ago.


00:19:39.767 --> 00:19:41.340
They are well-armed.


00:19:50.983 --> 00:19:52.187
And the Americans?


00:19:52.217 --> 00:19:55.657
No, sir.
I have not seen them.


00:19:55.687 --> 00:19:58.323
And she has
the algorithm for sure?


00:19:59.858 --> 00:20:01.360
<i>Oui.</i>


00:20:03.329 --> 00:20:05.298
What is he doing?


00:20:28.119 --> 00:20:29.990
Excellent work.


00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.691
Merci, sir.


00:20:31.721 --> 00:20:33.392
May I leave?


00:20:37.797 --> 00:20:39.966
You have five seconds
to run for your life.


00:20:39.996 --> 00:20:43.505
No! No, sir!


00:20:43.535 --> 00:20:46.705
Sir, no!
Please! No, no!


00:21:02.821 --> 00:21:05.257
Damn it!


00:21:06.358 --> 00:21:07.663
The traitor sold us out.


00:21:07.693 --> 00:21:09.829
Let's concentrate
on the task in hand.


00:21:09.859 --> 00:21:11.363
I count ten men.


00:21:11.393 --> 00:21:13.081
Same here, sir.


00:21:13.111 --> 00:21:14.770
Can we trust you?


00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:17.606
I risked my life
to fight the Germans!


00:21:17.636 --> 00:21:20.606
I watched as my mother
and father begged for their life


00:21:20.636 --> 00:21:23.542
and the life
of my brother and sister!


00:21:23.572 --> 00:21:26.449
They were only eight
and nine years old!


00:21:26.479 --> 00:21:28.547
They'll do the same thing
to her if we leave her.


00:21:28.577 --> 00:21:30.482
No one said anything
about leaving her.


00:21:30.512 --> 00:21:32.221
We heard the colonel, sir.


00:21:32.251 --> 00:21:34.220
You swear you have
the algorithm?


00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:35.788
It's all I have!


00:21:39.591 --> 00:21:42.130
We know you are in there!


00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.697
To the British
soldiers inside:


00:21:45.727 --> 00:21:47.065
Send us the girl


00:21:47.066 --> 00:21:48.568
and you will all go free.


00:21:58.211 --> 00:22:01.381
Otherwise, you will
experience the same fate


00:22:01.411 --> 00:22:04.184
as your French friend here.


00:22:09.387 --> 00:22:12.759
She will never give
the algorithm to the Allies.


00:22:12.789 --> 00:22:14.230
Ever!


00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:16.896
You send her out,
you will all go free!


00:22:22.769 --> 00:22:26.839
You have two minutes
to send her out.


00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:37.052
No.


00:22:37.082 --> 00:22:38.320
No, no, please!


00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:40.819
Please! Please!
I am telling the truth!


00:22:40.849 --> 00:22:41.857
Please!


00:22:41.887 --> 00:22:45.157
Please, you must
believe me! Please!


00:22:45.187 --> 00:22:46.658
Gentlemen?


00:22:54.366 --> 00:22:56.169
Speak freely, lads.
You heard the colonel.


00:22:56.199 --> 00:22:57.936
You know the mission.


00:23:09.415 --> 00:23:11.087
Well, I want to go home.


00:23:11.117 --> 00:23:13.554
We don't even know
if she has the algorithm.


00:23:13.584 --> 00:23:16.021
And how do we know
this algorithm can even do


00:23:16.051 --> 00:23:17.656
what people say
it can?


00:23:20.525 --> 00:23:22.461
Give her to them.


00:23:22.462 --> 00:23:23.829
How can we really trust her?


00:23:29.935 --> 00:23:33.539
I couldn't live with myself
if we turned her in, sir.


00:23:33.569 --> 00:23:36.677
Let's complete the mission.


00:23:36.707 --> 00:23:38.577
I've always thought it's
a soldier's duty


00:23:38.578 --> 00:23:40.846
to protect those who
can't protect themselves.


00:23:40.876 --> 00:23:43.381
Now there are ten of them
to our five,


00:23:43.411 --> 00:23:45.887
but we have
the elevated position.


00:23:45.917 --> 00:23:48.454
But, Lieutenant, they may
have reinforcements?


00:23:48.484 --> 00:23:50.091
Yes, that's quite possible,
Harris.


00:23:50.121 --> 00:23:53.124
But sometimes a man has
to take a stand on principle.


00:23:53.125 --> 00:23:55.728
No matter the consequences.


00:23:57.462 --> 00:23:58.901
I'm with you, sir.


00:23:58.931 --> 00:24:01.668
You say and I'll fill them
so full of lead,


00:24:01.698 --> 00:24:03.569
it'll be coming
out their eyes.


00:24:14.347 --> 00:24:16.351
Thank you, gentlemen.


00:24:16.381 --> 00:24:18.884
You will not regret this!
Thank you.


00:24:22.487 --> 00:24:24.491
All right,
Fritz, we've talked.


00:24:24.521 --> 00:24:26.495
We're not
bringing her out,


00:24:26.525 --> 00:24:28.827
so you're gonna have
to come in and get her!


00:24:28.828 --> 00:24:30.629
Fire!


00:24:41.106 --> 00:24:43.041
Pull out!


00:24:44.243 --> 00:24:45.778
Pull out!


00:24:49.381 --> 00:24:50.600
Patch him up, man.


00:24:50.630 --> 00:24:51.819
Am I gonna die?


00:24:51.849 --> 00:24:54.437
- No.
- Am I gonna die?


00:24:54.467 --> 00:24:57.056
Am I gonna die?
Shit!


00:24:57.086 --> 00:24:58.725
Am I gonna die?


00:25:12.303 --> 00:25:14.072
Damn it!


00:25:20.846 --> 00:25:22.982
Sir!
I have some dynamite!


00:25:23.012 --> 00:25:24.020
Let me set a trap.


00:25:24.050 --> 00:25:26.519
I'll blow these bastards
to smithereens.


00:25:31.057 --> 00:25:33.126
Schreck!
I've got a schreck here!


00:25:33.156 --> 00:25:34.797
God, then
we're out-gunned!


00:25:34.827 --> 00:25:37.499
We gotta get outta here!
Any ideas?


00:25:37.529 --> 00:25:39.330
Let's go out the back way!
I know the forest!


00:25:39.360 --> 00:25:40.933
King, Walker, on Thomas!


00:25:40.963 --> 00:25:42.170
Go!


00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:43.636
Thomas, let's go!


00:26:48.134 --> 00:26:50.903
Let's keep moving.
Come on.


00:26:50.933 --> 00:26:52.070
Chins up.


00:26:55.840 --> 00:26:58.144
That's it.
This way.


00:27:03.515 --> 00:27:06.017
All right, mighty forty,
everyone down here.


00:27:35.214 --> 00:27:36.682
Come on!


00:27:38.916 --> 00:27:41.190
Stay with me. Come on.


00:27:41.220 --> 00:27:43.923
We're getting out of here.
We're getting out of here.


00:27:51.496 --> 00:27:53.031
Come on!
Hold it together, Thomas!


00:27:53.061 --> 00:27:54.403
We've got to move on, man!


00:27:54.433 --> 00:27:56.935
We're working
on this together.


00:27:56.965 --> 00:27:59.204
Pull it together, Thomas.


00:29:16.181 --> 00:29:18.869
So any chance of getting
medical support for Thomas?


00:29:18.899 --> 00:29:22.113
The wireless was destroyed.
There's no calling anyone.


00:29:22.143 --> 00:29:25.357
Are you sure we can trust
this location that he gave us?


00:29:25.387 --> 00:29:27.128
<i>Oui.</i>


00:29:27.158 --> 00:29:29.593
I mean, he was working for the
Germans, it may be compromised.


00:29:29.623 --> 00:29:31.098
I don't think so.


00:29:31.128 --> 00:29:33.965
I don't think Pierre expected
us to escape. You know?


00:29:33.995 --> 00:29:36.204
Yes. You may have a point.


00:29:36.234 --> 00:29:38.435
Damn it, we need a radio!
We need to pause!


00:29:38.465 --> 00:29:39.587
I know a safe house.


00:29:39.617 --> 00:29:40.739
It might have a radio.


00:29:40.740 --> 00:29:42.907
- How far?
- Not far.


00:31:01.686 --> 00:31:05.627
- Shit!
- Sir!


00:31:05.657 --> 00:31:07.827
Sir, he's not doing so well.


00:31:12.364 --> 00:31:14.700
Sir, they're getting closer.
We'll never outrun them.


00:31:14.730 --> 00:31:16.234
Especially with him
in this state.


00:31:16.264 --> 00:31:17.769
Well, we can't
just leave him here!


00:31:17.799 --> 00:31:18.904
You are...


00:31:20.406 --> 00:31:24.046
You have to.


00:31:24.076 --> 00:31:26.278
I'm not going to make it.


00:31:26.308 --> 00:31:27.782
I know that.


00:31:27.812 --> 00:31:29.180
And you know that.


00:31:29.181 --> 00:31:31.801
This can't
be all for nothing.


00:31:31.831 --> 00:31:34.451
You said we could
be heroes.


00:31:34.452 --> 00:31:36.454
Now get her to safety!


00:31:37.356 --> 00:31:39.126
You're coming with us, Thomas.


00:31:39.156 --> 00:31:41.260
We're gonna get you home
to see your wife and son.


00:31:41.290 --> 00:31:45.731
You lads can do it,
but not with me.


00:31:45.761 --> 00:31:48.436
Not with me!


00:31:48.466 --> 00:31:50.953
You get home to England.


00:31:50.983 --> 00:31:53.471
You tell my son what I did.


00:31:53.472 --> 00:31:57.242
You tell him I was a hero.


00:31:57.272 --> 00:31:58.512
I shall.


00:31:58.542 --> 00:32:00.312
Reach into my pocket.


00:32:00.342 --> 00:32:02.530
- Here.
- This one?


00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:04.748
There. There's a letter.


00:32:04.749 --> 00:32:08.957
Please...


00:32:08.987 --> 00:32:11.489
Please give this
to my wife.


00:32:11.490 --> 00:32:13.825
You tell her...


00:32:17.229 --> 00:32:19.631
You tell her that
I loved her the minute


00:32:19.661 --> 00:32:22.267
I have laid eyes
on her.


00:32:22.268 --> 00:32:24.472
I promise.


00:32:24.502 --> 00:32:26.706
You keep that promise.


00:32:26.736 --> 00:32:28.940
I will.
I will, Thomas.


00:32:28.941 --> 00:32:31.446
All right. Now...


00:32:31.476 --> 00:32:35.480
Now sit me up
against that tree.


00:32:41.820 --> 00:32:44.290
And hand me my gun.


00:32:48.126 --> 00:32:50.295
You don't have
to do this, Thomas.


00:32:50.325 --> 00:32:51.896
Yes, I do.


00:32:53.531 --> 00:32:54.532
Now go!


00:32:56.268 --> 00:33:01.273
Monsieur, I'm so sorry.


00:33:01.303 --> 00:33:03.007
Go!


00:33:20.759 --> 00:33:23.165
Let's go.


00:33:23.195 --> 00:33:26.197
Come on, you bloody krauts!


00:35:53.077 --> 00:35:54.178
<i>Schiesse!</i>


00:36:08.861 --> 00:36:11.949
That'll slow 'em down.
But it won't stop 'em.


00:36:11.979 --> 00:36:15.067
If Angelique's secret is
as valuable as we think,


00:36:15.097 --> 00:36:17.471
- then nothing will stop them.
- It is.


00:36:17.501 --> 00:36:20.271
Well, at least Thomas has bought us
enough time to gain some distance.


00:36:20.272 --> 00:36:23.241
It's just north,
a few kilometers.


00:36:23.271 --> 00:36:24.911
Let's move on.


00:36:24.941 --> 00:36:27.278
Everyone stays alert.


00:36:41.059 --> 00:36:42.530
We need to rest.


00:36:42.560 --> 00:36:46.231
All right, let's stop
just for a moment.


00:36:48.899 --> 00:36:50.769
Be sure and conserve water.


00:36:55.138 --> 00:36:57.776
These blisters are
killing me.


00:37:04.983 --> 00:37:07.218
Sir, I've got
ammunition here!


00:37:07.248 --> 00:37:08.787
Stop! Freeze, King!


00:37:12.990 --> 00:37:15.759
Don't move.


00:37:15.760 --> 00:37:18.162
Shit!


00:37:20.964 --> 00:37:23.968
Is it booby trapped?


00:37:23.998 --> 00:37:25.239
Yes, sir.


00:37:25.269 --> 00:37:27.538
With a compression mine.


00:37:27.539 --> 00:37:30.542
Attached to a grenade.
A stick grenade, sir.


00:37:32.577 --> 00:37:34.279
Do you see where
it's connected?


00:37:34.309 --> 00:37:36.983
Yes, sir.


00:37:37.013 --> 00:37:39.186
About six feet to my left.


00:37:39.216 --> 00:37:41.619
Mr. King, I need you
to ever so slightly


00:37:41.620 --> 00:37:43.125
point to where
the grenade is.


00:37:43.155 --> 00:37:45.323
Don't move your head
or your hips at all.


00:37:45.353 --> 00:37:46.328
Do you understand?


00:37:46.358 --> 00:37:49.127
Just turn your
wrist and point.


00:38:14.318 --> 00:38:16.487
Do you see it?


00:38:16.488 --> 00:38:17.791
Yes.


00:38:17.821 --> 00:38:19.390
Yes, I see it.


00:38:22.059 --> 00:38:23.928
Could we cut the wire?


00:38:32.070 --> 00:38:34.924
I need you to stay
very, very still.


00:38:34.954 --> 00:38:37.808
We're going to get you
out of this.


00:38:37.809 --> 00:38:41.879
You have to absolutely
not budge in the slightest.


00:38:41.909 --> 00:38:43.515
Yes, sir.


00:38:54.359 --> 00:38:57.065
How bad is it?


00:38:57.095 --> 00:38:58.800
They've double-rigged it.


00:38:58.830 --> 00:39:01.533
There's a compression mine
under the butt of the rifle.


00:39:03.633 --> 00:39:05.870
As long as he keeps pressure
on that, it won't detonate.


00:39:05.900 --> 00:39:08.539
But the wire that's
attached to the grenade


00:39:08.569 --> 00:39:10.212
is already
under tension.


00:39:10.242 --> 00:39:13.312
We clip that,
the charge will blow.


00:39:16.147 --> 00:39:17.818
Shit.


00:39:17.848 --> 00:39:19.251
What do we do?


00:40:14.606 --> 00:40:16.941
I'm never going to be with
a woman now, am I, sir?


00:40:16.971 --> 00:40:18.179
Stay calm, Mr. King.


00:40:18.209 --> 00:40:20.396
We've got to do something.


00:40:20.426 --> 00:40:22.583
He's already struggling.


00:40:22.613 --> 00:40:24.883
Those Nazis can't
be too far back.


00:40:29.620 --> 00:40:31.525
What are you thinking, sir?


00:40:31.555 --> 00:40:33.691
The only thing I can do
is try to tackle him


00:40:33.721 --> 00:40:35.225
out of the blast area.


00:40:35.255 --> 00:40:36.663
That's insane!


00:40:36.693 --> 00:40:38.496
And keep your
voice down, man!


00:40:38.497 --> 00:40:40.201
We need to keep him
steady.


00:40:40.231 --> 00:40:42.098
Are you losing your mind,
Lieutenant.


00:40:42.128 --> 00:40:43.672
With all due respect, sir.


00:40:43.702 --> 00:40:45.639
Well, do you have
a better idea?


00:40:45.669 --> 00:40:47.256
If we had something
to dampen the blast,


00:40:47.286 --> 00:40:48.873
then that would be
a fine thing, but...


00:40:48.874 --> 00:40:52.644
Any branches we might find
would just add to the shrapnel.


00:40:55.412 --> 00:40:57.284
I think I can get him clear.


00:40:57.314 --> 00:41:02.253
Sergeant Walker, if you
would accompany me over here,


00:41:02.254 --> 00:41:04.422
we can deduce
the blast radius.


00:41:04.452 --> 00:41:07.059
What are best chances are.


00:41:11.062 --> 00:41:13.964
Appears to be a slightly
angled towards 11:00.


00:41:16.234 --> 00:41:18.572
This direction.


00:41:18.602 --> 00:41:21.041
A radius nearly five feet.


00:41:21.071 --> 00:41:25.042
Should have two to three
seconds before it goes.


00:41:36.053 --> 00:41:37.891
Shall we?


00:41:37.921 --> 00:41:39.875
Seek out cover,
Sergeant Walker.


00:41:39.905 --> 00:41:41.829
What are you going
to do, sir?


00:41:41.859 --> 00:41:44.995
Here's what we're
going to do, Mr. King.


00:41:48.733 --> 00:41:51.239
I am going to tackle you.


00:41:51.269 --> 00:41:53.574
You are going to stay
absolutely still


00:41:53.604 --> 00:41:55.573
until you feel
my body slamming into yours.


00:41:55.603 --> 00:41:56.710
Do you understand that?


00:41:56.740 --> 00:42:00.177
Pardon, sir?
What did you say?


00:42:00.178 --> 00:42:01.781
Tackle you, King.


00:42:01.811 --> 00:42:03.415
It's our only option.


00:42:11.388 --> 00:42:12.626
I don't want to die, sir.


00:42:12.656 --> 00:42:15.262
But I don't want you
to die either, sir.


00:42:15.292 --> 00:42:18.829
Maybe not. Just move on and I'll take
care of this. Don't worry about it.


00:42:18.830 --> 00:42:21.199
None of us is going
to die, King.


00:42:21.229 --> 00:42:22.536
I can do this.


00:42:22.566 --> 00:42:25.202
But I need you to let me
do the work.


00:42:25.232 --> 00:42:26.503
Do you understand?


00:42:26.504 --> 00:42:28.873
If you move, you cost us
precious milliseconds.


00:42:28.903 --> 00:42:32.543
Let me move you.
You understand?


00:42:34.345 --> 00:42:35.747
Yes, sir.


00:42:38.515 --> 00:42:41.185
When are you going
to do this, sir?


00:42:47.492 --> 00:42:49.560
I shall give you
plenty of warning.


00:42:49.590 --> 00:42:51.128
Don't worry, Mr. King.


00:42:54.064 --> 00:42:55.599
Maybe it's not such
a good idea, sir.


00:42:55.600 --> 00:42:57.702
I mean, we could always
just cut the wire...


00:43:27.731 --> 00:43:28.966
You all right?


00:43:33.470 --> 00:43:34.905
Damn!


00:43:37.075 --> 00:43:39.179
Sorry, sir.
It's my fault. I'm sorry.


00:43:39.209 --> 00:43:43.380
All right, that's enough,
I'm alive. You're alive.


00:43:43.381 --> 00:43:45.149
This is not good.


00:43:47.718 --> 00:43:48.855
Shit.


00:43:48.885 --> 00:43:50.454
What's the diagnosis, man?


00:43:50.455 --> 00:43:53.892
Well, the good news is
you've got a clean open wound.


00:43:53.922 --> 00:43:56.594
Probably some
shrapnel tearing through.


00:43:56.624 --> 00:43:59.067
The bad news is this branch.


00:43:59.097 --> 00:44:01.868
Not much bleeding
because it's an impalement.


00:44:01.898 --> 00:44:04.669
But could have lacerated
your femoral artery.


00:44:04.699 --> 00:44:08.573
And you'd bleed
to death internally.


00:44:08.603 --> 00:44:10.641
And how do we know that?


00:44:10.671 --> 00:44:12.646
You'll know.


00:44:12.676 --> 00:44:15.146
I'll just plug this hole.


00:44:16.147 --> 00:44:17.250
Stop the bleeding.


00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:22.853
And then if I dress
this branch to stabilize it.


00:44:22.854 --> 00:44:25.207
Just do as little as
you need to, Harris.


00:44:25.237 --> 00:44:27.900
We don't have much time.
That's an order.


00:44:27.930 --> 00:44:30.593
It's good the house
is not far off, sir.


00:44:30.623 --> 00:44:32.731
Quick as you can, man.


00:44:36.600 --> 00:44:38.604
Can you walk?


00:44:38.634 --> 00:44:40.638
Yes. I can try.


00:44:40.668 --> 00:44:42.307
Come on.


00:46:45.296 --> 00:46:46.733
This is it.


00:46:46.763 --> 00:46:48.201
How are you doing, sir?


00:46:48.231 --> 00:46:50.500
Still planning on
surviving this bloody war.


00:46:50.501 --> 00:46:52.755
Are you sure this
place is safe?


00:46:52.785 --> 00:46:55.039
I'm not sure about
anything anymore,


00:46:55.069 --> 00:46:57.241
but what choice
do we have?


00:46:57.271 --> 00:46:59.709
Let's go.


00:47:17.829 --> 00:47:20.365
Come in. Quickly.
Quickly.


00:47:24.001 --> 00:47:25.335
Come on, sir.


00:47:28.338 --> 00:47:29.610
Come on.


00:47:29.640 --> 00:47:31.776
Easy, sir, easy.


00:47:40.885 --> 00:47:41.952
You quite all right,
Mr. Harris?


00:47:41.982 --> 00:47:43.123
Yes, sir, just need...


00:47:43.153 --> 00:47:45.192
Let me help.
I was a nurse.


00:47:45.222 --> 00:47:47.225
I worked at Clemenceau
Hospital before it was bombed.


00:47:47.255 --> 00:47:48.593
You...
you have a radio, yes?


00:47:48.623 --> 00:47:49.931
<i>Oui.</i>


00:47:49.961 --> 00:47:52.281
But it only hails frequencies
from the Resistance.


00:47:52.311 --> 00:47:54.631
Well, I mean, is there any
way that the Resistance


00:47:54.661 --> 00:47:56.600
can get in touch with
the allies so they can


00:47:56.630 --> 00:47:58.385
let them know our whereabouts?


00:47:58.415 --> 00:48:00.141
It is possible.
I can try.


00:48:00.171 --> 00:48:02.239
All right, Harris,
you accompany our friend


00:48:02.269 --> 00:48:03.675
and see if you
can achieve that.


00:48:10.948 --> 00:48:13.050
Because this did not
hit an artery,


00:48:13.051 --> 00:48:14.355
we can remove it.


00:48:14.385 --> 00:48:16.254
And you know this how,
from your time as a nurse?


00:48:16.284 --> 00:48:19.089
I shall get
some boiling water.


00:48:22.093 --> 00:48:23.697
Sir?


00:48:23.727 --> 00:48:25.766
Thank you.


00:48:25.796 --> 00:48:27.835
I was just doing my job.


00:48:27.865 --> 00:48:32.435
No, no, it's much more than just
doing your job saving my life.


00:48:32.465 --> 00:48:34.141
You're welcome, King.


00:48:34.171 --> 00:48:38.475
So, how's it going with
the French Resistance there?


00:48:38.505 --> 00:48:39.880
No.


00:48:39.910 --> 00:48:41.430
It's, it's
not like that.


00:48:41.460 --> 00:48:42.981
I'm sure
it's not, sir.


00:49:00.597 --> 00:49:02.466
This was a
good field dressing.


00:49:04.301 --> 00:49:06.571
I'll just leave her
to tend to your wounds, sir.


00:49:07.805 --> 00:49:09.009
What?


00:49:09.039 --> 00:49:12.547
Nothing.
He's just being an idiot.


00:49:12.577 --> 00:49:16.481
He's just a little boy who
needs the love of a woman.


00:49:16.511 --> 00:49:18.281
Yeah.


00:49:22.887 --> 00:49:24.821
F13C, come in, over.


00:49:27.624 --> 00:49:29.425
Is F13C checked in yet?


00:49:29.426 --> 00:49:31.012
Negative, sir.


00:49:31.042 --> 00:49:32.571
Raise them.


00:49:32.601 --> 00:49:34.131
Yes, sir.


00:49:38.736 --> 00:49:40.422
Okay, this is going to hurt.


00:49:40.452 --> 00:49:42.138
I wish I had
some whiskey or...


00:49:42.168 --> 00:49:43.556
I never touch the stuff.


00:49:43.586 --> 00:49:44.975
- No? Really?
- Really.


00:49:45.005 --> 00:49:47.311
Why not?


00:49:47.312 --> 00:49:48.315
It's okay. It's...


00:49:48.345 --> 00:49:49.847
it's none of my business.


00:49:51.347 --> 00:49:54.684
My father was rather
too fond of the stuff.


00:49:54.714 --> 00:49:56.453
Wasn't a great man.


00:50:00.091 --> 00:50:02.259
You're a great man.


00:50:02.289 --> 00:50:04.030
No.


00:50:04.060 --> 00:50:05.329
No, I'm just a soldier.


00:50:05.330 --> 00:50:08.066
No. You are so much
more than that.


00:50:16.506 --> 00:50:18.309
I'm sorry. I...


00:50:20.912 --> 00:50:22.946
God, that hurt.


00:50:22.976 --> 00:50:24.351
I'm sorry.


00:50:24.381 --> 00:50:26.050
I thought it was better
to take you by surprise.


00:50:26.080 --> 00:50:27.785
Well, you certainly did that.


00:50:27.815 --> 00:50:30.757
Dear God, that smarts.


00:50:30.787 --> 00:50:34.191
Okay, put pressure on there.


00:50:37.695 --> 00:50:39.196
Hold it.


00:50:49.906 --> 00:50:51.609
Thank you
for trusting me.


00:51:07.925 --> 00:51:09.926
I'll say this
for these Frenchmen:


00:51:09.956 --> 00:51:12.030
they make
a damn good wine.


00:51:13.765 --> 00:51:15.966
I'm a beer man,
myself.


00:51:15.996 --> 00:51:17.901
When in Rome.


00:51:17.931 --> 00:51:19.806
Drink up.


00:51:19.836 --> 00:51:22.472
You never know
when you...


00:51:27.412 --> 00:51:28.479
Right.


00:51:38.722 --> 00:51:41.492
Have you really never
been with a woman?


00:51:45.196 --> 00:51:48.766
Well, I mean
I've kissed 'em.


00:51:48.796 --> 00:51:49.737
Lots of them.


00:51:49.767 --> 00:51:53.088
But, no,
not all the way.


00:51:53.118 --> 00:51:56.439
You're missing out, mate.


00:51:56.469 --> 00:51:58.078
Well...


00:51:58.108 --> 00:52:00.611
To me,
it's not just about sex.


00:52:03.379 --> 00:52:08.051
The more you have of a thing,
the less special it becomes.


00:52:08.081 --> 00:52:11.190
At least to me.


00:52:11.220 --> 00:52:13.156
I've always wanted it
to be with the right woman.


00:52:13.186 --> 00:52:16.394
Mate, they're all
the right woman.


00:52:21.966 --> 00:52:23.471
Hey, to be honest
with you,


00:52:23.501 --> 00:52:26.537
my first time I was
head over heels in love.


00:52:29.906 --> 00:52:33.778
We were just kids with
no idea what we were doing.


00:52:37.714 --> 00:52:39.216
But it was real.


00:52:49.526 --> 00:52:51.596
I can't imagine what I'm going
to tell Mrs. Thomas.


00:52:55.298 --> 00:52:58.034
You are going to tell her
that her man was a hero,


00:52:58.035 --> 00:53:01.406
and we wouldn't be here
if he hadn't done what he did.


00:53:03.073 --> 00:53:05.409
And if you want,
I'll go with you.


00:53:07.477 --> 00:53:09.780
Thank you.


00:53:15.285 --> 00:53:17.187
You're a good man,
Mr. Walker.


00:53:18.988 --> 00:53:22.592
No. I'm not.


00:53:24.928 --> 00:53:26.696
But I'm trying.


00:53:30.667 --> 00:53:32.670
You have your moments.


00:53:32.700 --> 00:53:34.704
All it takes is one.


00:53:35.838 --> 00:53:37.808
One good one.


00:53:42.245 --> 00:53:44.714
You should wait
for the right woman, King.


00:54:37.734 --> 00:54:41.037
F13C, this is 7, 8,
Echo, Charlie, Papa.


00:54:41.067 --> 00:54:42.710
Come in, over.


00:54:42.740 --> 00:54:48.946
Again, F13C,
this is 78ECP.


00:54:48.976 --> 00:54:50.247
Come in, over.


00:54:51.649 --> 00:54:53.484
There... there's
no response, sir.


00:54:53.514 --> 00:54:55.819
- Keep scanning.
- Yes, sir.


00:55:05.629 --> 00:55:07.735
F13C here.


00:55:07.765 --> 00:55:09.170
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:12.836
Repeat, F13C,
are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:12.866 --> 00:55:14.907
F13C here.


00:55:14.937 --> 00:55:17.273
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:17.274 --> 00:55:20.012
Repeat, F13C here.


00:55:20.042 --> 00:55:22.046
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:22.076 --> 00:55:23.847
F13C, come in.


00:55:29.320 --> 00:55:30.590
Keep searching.


00:55:30.620 --> 00:55:32.656
He may be using
a different frequency.


00:55:35.892 --> 00:55:37.963
<i>F13C here.</i>


00:55:37.993 --> 00:55:39.829
<i>Are you there, Dunkirk?</i>


00:55:39.830 --> 00:55:41.201
We have a signal, sir.


00:55:41.231 --> 00:55:43.835
<i>F13C here.
Are you there, Dunkirk?</i>


00:55:43.865 --> 00:55:46.469
F13C.
This is Colonel Plummer.


00:55:46.470 --> 00:55:48.842
<i>What is your sitrep?</i>


00:55:48.872 --> 00:55:51.045
Repeat, what is your sitrep?


00:55:51.075 --> 00:55:55.212
We're at a safe house,
outside the drop coordinates,


00:55:55.242 --> 00:55:58.131
approximately
four miles northwest.


00:55:58.161 --> 00:56:01.051
Good to hear
your voices, boys.


00:56:01.081 --> 00:56:02.188
What's your situation?


00:56:02.218 --> 00:56:04.554
<i>We've lost Sgt. Thomas.</i>


00:56:04.555 --> 00:56:06.525
<i>Lieutenant Calloway
is injured,</i>


00:56:06.555 --> 00:56:08.496
but we have
secured the package.


00:56:08.526 --> 00:56:10.665
<i>We're being pursued
by Jerrys, sir.</i>


00:56:10.695 --> 00:56:13.132
<i>We're possibly going
to need air support.</i>


00:56:13.162 --> 00:56:16.733
French Resistance have had
a change of plans, so we...


00:56:16.763 --> 00:56:18.669
we may have
been compromised.


00:56:19.903 --> 00:56:21.775
Where are you heading?


00:56:21.805 --> 00:56:26.344
<i>We're heading to an airfield
about two miles from the bridge.</i>


00:56:26.374 --> 00:56:28.681
<i>The package will be
flown to mainland.</i>


00:56:28.711 --> 00:56:30.516
<i>Sir, we're going
to have to pass through</i>


00:56:30.546 --> 00:56:33.282
<i>German-occupied area
to get to the airfield.</i>


00:56:33.283 --> 00:56:34.721
<i>We may need support.</i>


00:56:34.751 --> 00:56:38.607
I'll do my best
to provide some air support.


00:56:38.637 --> 00:56:42.493
Pop some smoke so
we know where you are.


00:56:42.523 --> 00:56:43.496
<i>One more thing.</i>


00:56:43.526 --> 00:56:45.065
What's that, Colonel?


00:56:45.095 --> 00:56:48.703
There should be a bridge a few
kilometers down the main route.


00:56:48.733 --> 00:56:52.970
<i>We have reason to believe there's a
German patrol operating in that area.</i>


00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:57.041
<i>That would put a group of French
freedom fighters in danger.</i>


00:56:57.071 --> 00:57:01.410
I want you boys
to blow that bridge.


00:57:01.440 --> 00:57:02.882
But with what, sir?


00:57:02.912 --> 00:57:06.516
Walker should have
the explosives you boys need.


00:57:06.517 --> 00:57:09.287
Roger that. Out.


00:57:14.591 --> 00:57:17.560
Tell headquarters we should
send men to the bridge


00:57:17.590 --> 00:57:20.097
and to the airstrip.


00:57:32.108 --> 00:57:33.877
We have more company.


00:57:48.291 --> 00:57:49.693
Quietly.


00:57:57.033 --> 00:57:58.237
That's gotta sting.


00:57:58.267 --> 00:57:59.620
Mr. Keller, do you drink?


00:57:59.650 --> 00:58:01.004
As much as I can, ma'am.


00:58:07.044 --> 00:58:09.946
This looks like
it's going to be fine.


00:58:09.976 --> 00:58:11.083
I'll live.


00:58:11.113 --> 00:58:12.416
We'll all will.


00:58:33.303 --> 00:58:35.857
Do you see any more?


00:58:35.887 --> 00:58:38.441
Let's hide the bodies.


00:58:43.314 --> 00:58:45.049
<i>Nein.</i>


00:58:59.028 --> 00:59:01.097
<i>Ja wohl.</i>


00:59:11.106 --> 00:59:12.275
You talked to the Colonel?


00:59:12.276 --> 00:59:14.614
- Yes.
- What does he say?


00:59:14.644 --> 00:59:16.280
I managed to give him
our coordinates and then...


00:59:16.310 --> 00:59:17.451
We're out of time, sir.


00:59:17.481 --> 00:59:19.186
Why?
What's... what's happening?


00:59:19.216 --> 00:59:21.785
We just killed two Nazis who were
about to call in our position.


00:59:21.815 --> 00:59:23.757
- Damn it.
- Can you walk?


00:59:23.787 --> 00:59:25.388
Doesn't look like
I have much choice, does it?


00:59:25.418 --> 00:59:27.607
Come on, sir.
Come on.


00:59:27.637 --> 00:59:29.826
That's it.
All right.


00:59:29.827 --> 00:59:31.729
<i>Merci.</i>


00:59:46.042 --> 00:59:49.211
The airfield is
15 kilometers north.


00:59:49.241 --> 00:59:50.250
<i>Merci.</i>


00:59:50.280 --> 00:59:51.518
<i>Merci beaucoup.</i>


00:59:51.548 --> 00:59:53.654
So, yeah, thank you
for what you are doing.


00:59:53.684 --> 00:59:56.252
The Nazis are coming. You cannot
stay here, you know that.


00:59:56.282 --> 00:59:57.556
I know.


00:59:57.586 --> 00:59:59.956
I'm going to try
and buy you some more time.


01:00:01.124 --> 01:00:02.593
<i>Merci.</i>


01:00:03.993 --> 01:00:05.829
Sir, are you sure you don't
want any of that morphine?


01:00:05.859 --> 01:00:08.064
No, thank you, Harris.
It dulls the senses.


01:00:08.094 --> 01:00:10.300
Yeah, but so does having
a tree in your leg.


01:01:04.187 --> 01:01:05.891
<i>Bonjour.</i>


01:01:05.921 --> 01:01:07.625
No, no, no.


01:01:16.934 --> 01:01:20.137
It's a rather nice day
for a stroll, isn't it?


01:01:23.205 --> 01:01:26.709
And where is our French
little mouse strolling to?


01:01:32.548 --> 01:01:35.818
We can make this so much simpler
if you just tell me where she is.


01:01:37.620 --> 01:01:38.590
Who?


01:01:38.620 --> 01:01:40.791
What girl?


01:01:43.258 --> 01:01:45.162
Bring him.


01:01:45.192 --> 01:01:47.197
No, no.


01:01:47.227 --> 01:01:49.233
Wait. Wait.


01:01:52.669 --> 01:01:55.705
I don't under...
What is going...


01:03:08.512 --> 01:03:11.749
I love the smell
of burning flesh.


01:03:14.684 --> 01:03:19.326
It reminds me of how,
as a little boy,


01:03:19.356 --> 01:03:24.093
<i>my father would roast
a schwein on an open fire.</i>


01:03:32.769 --> 01:03:35.272
Now, tell me where they are.


01:03:39.575 --> 01:03:42.945
I don't know what
you're talking about.


01:04:05.328 --> 01:04:08.197
Now tell me everything
or you will die.


01:04:09.132 --> 01:04:12.535
Okay, okay.


01:04:15.838 --> 01:04:17.974
Everything, I'll tell you.


01:04:21.043 --> 01:04:24.084
They are...


01:04:24.114 --> 01:04:26.250
heading into the village.


01:04:32.188 --> 01:04:37.027
Now, why would they
be going into a village


01:04:37.057 --> 01:04:40.230
that is crawling
with Germans?


01:04:42.931 --> 01:04:45.971
Ex... exactly.


01:04:46.001 --> 01:04:49.405
That is the last place you
would expect to see them.


01:04:52.175 --> 01:04:56.780
Do I look,
stupid to you?


01:04:56.810 --> 01:04:58.648
Honest answer?


01:05:02.918 --> 01:05:04.187
<i>Oui.</i>


01:05:08.491 --> 01:05:10.427
So be it.


01:05:14.797 --> 01:05:18.901
For your information,
I know that the girl


01:05:18.902 --> 01:05:24.441
is trying to escape by plane
from a small airfield.


01:05:27.943 --> 01:05:30.146
Not so stupid now, am I?


01:06:21.533 --> 01:06:23.336
Do you need to stop?


01:06:25.870 --> 01:06:27.506
Perhaps just
for a moment.


01:06:35.113 --> 01:06:38.353
By my calculations,
we are here,


01:06:38.383 --> 01:06:41.186
so it should be just
beyond this next ridge.


01:06:41.216 --> 01:06:42.921
You're never gonna
make it on that leg.


01:06:42.951 --> 01:06:44.522
That's at least
another six miles.


01:06:44.552 --> 01:06:45.627
I'll manage.


01:06:45.657 --> 01:06:47.894
You may not have to.


01:06:50.528 --> 01:06:52.097
What do you mean?


01:06:54.300 --> 01:06:55.802
Well, shit.


01:06:55.832 --> 01:06:57.335
Take cover.


01:07:17.122 --> 01:07:19.023
You know, I could probably
just pick him off


01:07:19.024 --> 01:07:21.426
from about a hundred
yards with this rifle.


01:07:21.456 --> 01:07:23.628
You snipers are
all the same.


01:07:23.629 --> 01:07:27.633
Trust me, mate, these blokes
will piss their pants.


01:07:27.663 --> 01:07:29.702
Yes, well, we'll see
about that, won't we?


01:07:52.289 --> 01:07:54.159
Be ready,
here they come.


01:08:10.108 --> 01:08:13.980
Help! Help!


01:08:15.213 --> 01:08:17.314
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot.


01:08:17.315 --> 01:08:19.018
Please, no, don't shoot.


01:08:19.048 --> 01:08:20.751
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot.


01:08:20.752 --> 01:08:22.488
Don't shoot me.
Please, no, don't shoot.


01:08:22.518 --> 01:08:24.522
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot, please.


01:08:24.552 --> 01:08:26.492
Hello, mates.


01:08:33.164 --> 01:08:35.368
Good afternoon, gentlemen.


01:08:39.538 --> 01:08:41.075
I can't believe
that worked.


01:08:41.105 --> 01:08:42.940
What would you do
if a big bald bastard


01:08:42.970 --> 01:08:45.043
tossed a grenade
in your vehicle?


01:08:45.073 --> 01:08:46.511
Fair point.


01:09:20.078 --> 01:09:21.597
It's quiet.
I don't like it.


01:09:21.627 --> 01:09:23.117
This should do the trick.


01:09:23.147 --> 01:09:24.516
Once we destroy it,
that should slow them down.


01:09:24.546 --> 01:09:25.783
- Mr. Harris?
- Sir?


01:09:25.813 --> 01:09:27.051
You stay and look out.


01:09:27.052 --> 01:09:29.187
Mr. King, Mr. Walker, would
you kindly assist me in rigging?


01:09:29.217 --> 01:09:30.955
The pleasure would
be mine, sir.


01:09:30.985 --> 01:09:32.361
Come along, King.


01:09:32.391 --> 01:09:34.827
You seem to like
explosives today.


01:10:44.195 --> 01:10:45.829
How are we doing, gentlemen?


01:10:45.859 --> 01:10:47.882
Getting there, sir.


01:10:47.912 --> 01:10:49.905
Sergeant Walker?


01:10:49.935 --> 01:10:51.602
A few more moments, please.


01:10:51.632 --> 01:10:52.704
Very well.


01:10:56.541 --> 01:10:58.709
How's it going
down there, chaps?


01:10:58.739 --> 01:11:00.028
Almost done.


01:11:00.058 --> 01:11:01.347
Make it quick.


01:11:04.583 --> 01:11:08.057
Is this the bridge?
Here?


01:11:08.087 --> 01:11:09.958
The open space on the other
side of this tree line


01:11:09.988 --> 01:11:13.191
has a hangar-like structure.
It's got to be the way out.


01:11:14.626 --> 01:11:16.429
Sir, if I'm reading
this map correctly,


01:11:16.459 --> 01:11:18.262
then the airfield
should just be on


01:11:18.292 --> 01:11:19.735
the other side of this forest.


01:11:19.765 --> 01:11:21.699
- Where's Walker and King?
- Just finishing up.


01:11:21.729 --> 01:11:23.135
They should be up
momentarily.


01:11:23.165 --> 01:11:24.436
I hope so.


01:11:28.006 --> 01:11:28.977
Do you hear that?


01:11:29.007 --> 01:11:30.379
That doesn't sound good.


01:11:30.409 --> 01:11:32.311
Doesn't sound like
a lot of fun.


01:11:32.341 --> 01:11:33.912
Mr. Walker?


01:11:33.913 --> 01:11:35.147
How are we
doing down there?


01:11:35.177 --> 01:11:36.584
Almost there, sir.


01:11:36.614 --> 01:11:39.385
Well, hurry up!
We have to go!


01:11:48.327 --> 01:11:50.529
- Start the car.
- It won't start, sir.


01:11:50.559 --> 01:11:51.932
Quick as you can, man.


01:11:51.962 --> 01:11:53.631
It won't start, sir.
It won't start.


01:11:53.632 --> 01:11:55.768
- Let's go!
- It won't start.


01:12:16.521 --> 01:12:19.890
Drop your weapons
and surrender.


01:12:19.891 --> 01:12:22.498
You have nowhere to go.


01:12:22.528 --> 01:12:26.049
It's a bloody tank.
Damn it.


01:12:26.079 --> 01:12:29.601
This is your final warning.


01:12:31.569 --> 01:12:34.271
Drop your weapons
and surrender.


01:12:34.301 --> 01:12:36.941
Damn, it's a ruddy tank!


01:12:39.177 --> 01:12:41.145
- We'll have to go on foot!
- Let's go!


01:12:43.181 --> 01:12:44.483
Go, go, go!


01:12:46.217 --> 01:12:49.120
Fire!


01:13:49.780 --> 01:13:52.984
Did you really think that
you could escape from me?


01:13:53.014 --> 01:13:55.821
We monitored
your radio transmissions.


01:15:12.965 --> 01:15:14.401
Are we good?


01:15:14.431 --> 01:15:15.868
We're good.


01:15:28.012 --> 01:15:30.614
I do not understand
how anyone could like


01:15:30.644 --> 01:15:32.784
such an inferior race.


01:15:34.520 --> 01:15:37.190
They're all like rats.


01:15:37.220 --> 01:15:39.861
Don't you know this?


01:15:39.891 --> 01:15:43.261
All they have
ever done was lie,


01:15:43.291 --> 01:15:46.031
steal, and cheat.


01:15:47.565 --> 01:15:49.635
And you support them?


01:15:51.435 --> 01:15:56.807
Now, we could have easily
slaughtered you Brits at Dunkirk.


01:15:56.837 --> 01:15:59.843
But we offered you
a second chance,


01:15:59.873 --> 01:16:02.817
a chance to align with us.


01:16:02.847 --> 01:16:07.151
Let's just see if your
Mr. Winston Churchill


01:16:07.181 --> 01:16:09.223
makes the right decision.


01:16:09.253 --> 01:16:12.441
If it were up to me,
I would have killed


01:16:12.471 --> 01:16:15.660
every last one
of you on that beach.


01:16:16.961 --> 01:16:19.998
But you will all
die here today.


01:16:21.365 --> 01:16:23.135
Do you realize this?


01:16:27.437 --> 01:16:29.173
And I will decide how.


01:16:33.677 --> 01:16:37.414
And as for you, French,


01:16:37.444 --> 01:16:39.984
you disgust me!


01:16:52.597 --> 01:16:55.851
Now personally, I would love


01:16:55.881 --> 01:16:59.136
to kill you
right here and now.


01:17:03.408 --> 01:17:06.313
But apparently...


01:17:06.343 --> 01:17:12.216
You have some information in that
French little brain of yours.


01:17:17.721 --> 01:17:22.293
That is very valuable
to us.


01:17:30.101 --> 01:17:33.972
Now, I will ask you
one simple question


01:17:35.873 --> 01:17:38.609
and you will answer me.


01:17:40.377 --> 01:17:42.647
What is the algorithm?


01:18:02.734 --> 01:18:07.873
What is the algorithm!?


01:18:09.440 --> 01:18:11.042
Bitch.


01:18:15.547 --> 01:18:17.384
I will count down from five,


01:18:17.414 --> 01:18:19.283
and then you will tell me
the algorithm.


01:18:21.720 --> 01:18:23.387
Okay. I will tell you!
I will tell you.


01:18:23.417 --> 01:18:24.655
Don't tell him anything!


01:18:28.927 --> 01:18:29.962
<i>Zwei.</i>


01:18:31.930 --> 01:18:32.897
<i>Eins.</i>


01:19:44.235 --> 01:19:46.337
You go on ahead.
I'll catch you up.


01:19:46.367 --> 01:19:47.538
Let me help you, sir.


01:19:54.445 --> 01:19:55.980
Fire!


01:19:58.583 --> 01:20:00.352
Cover and fire!


01:20:17.903 --> 01:20:19.870
Take cover!


01:20:43.761 --> 01:20:45.199
You all right, Mr. King?


01:20:45.229 --> 01:20:47.298
Yes, sir, just a nick.
I'm fine.


01:20:49.699 --> 01:20:51.736
All right.
Stay low. Stay low.


01:20:53.870 --> 01:20:55.873
We need to slow them down.


01:21:19.931 --> 01:21:21.832
You have nowhere to go!


01:21:21.862 --> 01:21:23.769
Surrender!


01:21:25.369 --> 01:21:27.805
More tension.
More tension.


01:21:29.539 --> 01:21:34.311
Surrender and give us the girl
and you will all go free.


01:21:38.882 --> 01:21:41.103
You will not escape.


01:21:41.133 --> 01:21:43.324
You will not get away.


01:21:43.354 --> 01:21:46.057
No one's going
to surrender, Fritz.


01:21:53.064 --> 01:21:54.499
How we doing, lads?


01:21:54.529 --> 01:21:56.534
One minute.


01:22:08.846 --> 01:22:10.985
Surrender!


01:22:11.015 --> 01:22:13.118
Okay, we're so close.


01:22:14.319 --> 01:22:15.255
Ready, sir.


01:22:15.285 --> 01:22:17.057
You will not
get out of there.


01:22:17.087 --> 01:22:19.423
Lay down covering fire
and move on my three,


01:22:19.453 --> 01:22:21.825
two, one... fire!


01:22:27.966 --> 01:22:29.151
Shit.


01:22:29.181 --> 01:22:30.367
Move!


01:22:31.970 --> 01:22:33.571
Move! Move!


01:22:34.672 --> 01:22:36.474
Go, go, go.


01:24:12.602 --> 01:24:14.541
For King and country.


01:24:14.571 --> 01:24:16.541
I'm willing to bet
Fritz is still coming.


01:24:16.571 --> 01:24:18.142
So let's go.


01:24:25.917 --> 01:24:27.254
Where is the plane?


01:24:27.284 --> 01:24:28.586
It's supposed to be here.


01:24:37.528 --> 01:24:39.129
No!


01:24:58.682 --> 01:25:00.284
You have nowhere to go!


01:25:06.157 --> 01:25:08.196
Surrender.


01:25:08.226 --> 01:25:11.996
Brother by my side,
what do you want to do?


01:25:12.026 --> 01:25:13.897
I have one magazine left.


01:25:13.927 --> 01:25:15.602
No. No.


01:25:15.632 --> 01:25:17.767
Drop your weapons.


01:25:17.797 --> 01:25:19.503
Do it now!


01:25:24.342 --> 01:25:27.045
You are totally surrounded.


01:25:29.779 --> 01:25:31.515
Bloody hell, I'm not
going out like this.


01:25:31.516 --> 01:25:33.718
- No!
- Stand down, Sergeant Walker.


01:25:33.748 --> 01:25:35.519
It's our only chance.


01:25:39.989 --> 01:25:41.960
I'm sorry, Angelique.


01:25:41.990 --> 01:25:43.660
We did all we could.


01:25:43.690 --> 01:25:45.145
Please, no.
Please, no.


01:25:45.175 --> 01:25:46.601
Please don't give up hope.


01:25:46.631 --> 01:25:49.367
It wasn't supposed
to end like this.


01:25:51.401 --> 01:25:52.703
Fire.


01:25:54.004 --> 01:25:56.106
Look. Look!


01:26:02.113 --> 01:26:03.785
It's our boys.


01:26:03.815 --> 01:26:05.717
It's about bloody time.


01:26:50.962 --> 01:26:52.530
<i>Schiesse.</i>


01:26:54.030 --> 01:26:55.833
<i>Schiesse.</i>


01:27:50.120 --> 01:27:53.856
See, you never
give up hope.


01:27:53.886 --> 01:27:55.396
We did it.


01:27:55.426 --> 01:27:58.631
God save the King.


01:27:58.661 --> 01:28:01.866
We did it.
We did it!


01:28:10.574 --> 01:28:11.879
Let's get her to that plane.


01:28:11.909 --> 01:28:14.679
You took the words
right out of my mouth.


01:29:00.056 --> 01:29:01.693
Thank you.


01:29:03.159 --> 01:29:04.695
Thank you.


01:29:06.596 --> 01:29:08.131
I'm sorry for your men.


01:29:08.132 --> 01:29:10.538
But thank you for my life.


01:29:10.568 --> 01:29:13.271
I just hope it
was worth it, love.


01:29:13.301 --> 01:29:15.439
It is.


01:29:20.444 --> 01:29:22.115
Could you do us a favor?


01:29:22.145 --> 01:29:25.581
When you get back to London,
find Emily Thomas.


01:29:25.582 --> 01:29:27.687
Give her this letter.


01:29:27.717 --> 01:29:29.820
I don't think I'll be around
to give it to her.


01:29:29.850 --> 01:29:31.954
And I'd rather she got it
sooner than later.


01:29:31.984 --> 01:29:33.456
Of course.


01:29:33.486 --> 01:29:34.958
Thank you.


01:29:39.663 --> 01:29:42.499
Let's get you on that plane.


01:29:42.529 --> 01:29:44.502
Are you all right?


01:29:44.532 --> 01:29:46.240
You?


01:29:46.270 --> 01:29:48.342
I'm alive.


01:29:48.372 --> 01:29:50.559
I don't know how,
but I am.


01:29:50.589 --> 01:29:52.746
You must never
give up hope.


01:29:52.776 --> 01:29:55.863
It doesn't matter how,
it matters why.


01:29:55.893 --> 01:29:58.981
You are a special man,
Lieutenant.


01:29:59.011 --> 01:30:00.916
You have a purpose.


01:30:00.946 --> 01:30:02.852
You must trust that.


01:30:02.882 --> 01:30:04.592
Thank you.


01:30:04.622 --> 01:30:07.527
Those men died heroes.


01:30:07.557 --> 01:30:09.694
Is there a better way
to serve your country?


01:30:09.724 --> 01:30:11.264
None.


01:30:11.294 --> 01:30:13.115
What will you do now?


01:30:13.145 --> 01:30:14.966
Will I see you again?


01:30:17.235 --> 01:30:19.272
This war is
far from over.


01:30:19.302 --> 01:30:24.240
I'll just have to enjoy the
beauty this world has to offer.


01:30:24.270 --> 01:30:27.912
When one remembers to
look beyond the ugliness.


01:30:44.294 --> 01:30:46.032
I'll see you in London.


01:30:46.062 --> 01:30:48.833
Now, let's get you
on that plane.


01:31:38.815 --> 01:31:40.583
I think she
likes you, sir.


01:31:40.613 --> 01:31:42.885
I don't know.


01:31:42.886 --> 01:31:45.323
Did you see the way
she looked at me just now?


01:31:45.353 --> 01:31:47.291
There might be
a real future there.


01:31:50.321 --> 01:32:08.321
<font color=#ff0000>subs4free.info</font>

